# apps/mobile uses Expo's Continuous Native Generation (CNG): the native
# projects are GENERATED from app.json + the config plugins, never hand-edited
# and never committed. `expo prebuild` and `eas build` regenerate them on demand.
#
# These entries are load-bearing. Before they existed, `expo prebuild` left
# ios/ and android/ as untracked-but-not-ignored, one `git add .` away from
# being committed — which would silently convert this app to the bare workflow.
# In bare, app.json's plugin block stops driving native config and every future
# SDK upgrade becomes a manual native merge instead of a regeneration. That is
# the single most expensive accident available in this directory.
#
# If the project ever adopts bare deliberately, delete these lines in the same
# commit that adds the native projects, so the switch is explicit and reviewable.
/ios/
/android/

# Expo local state
.expo/
expo-env.d.ts
